urt's Loper Bright decision.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2025/06/hipaas-reproductive-health-rule-is-vacated-nationally", "label": "Holland & Knight, HIPAA's reproductive health rule vacated nationally"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "survived", "eyebrow": "What remains", "title": "Privacy notice updates", "body": "Changes to notices of privacy practices for substance use disorder records stayed in effect.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Notice of Privacy Practices", "definition": "A document explaining how a provider uses and shares patient information."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2025/06/hipaas-reproductive-health-rule-is-vacated-nationally", "label": "Holland & Knight, HIPAA's reproductive health rule vacated nationally"}]}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "What happened to the 2024 reproductive health privacy rule?", "left": {"name": "Vacated nationwide", "note": "June 2025"}, "right": {"name": "Upheld and expanded", "note": "By Congress"}, "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A federal court vacated it nationwide on June 18, 2025."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You are a compliance officer at a clinic after the June 2025 ruling.", "prompt": "What do you still need to do?", "options": ["Update notices for addiction records", "Keep enforcing the vacated rule", "Stop all HIPAA compliance work"], "consequences": ["That part survived, with a February 2026 deadline.", "The vacated parts no longer apply.", "The rest of HIPAA still applies."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "The notice updates for substance use disorder records remained in effect."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Gone after a year", "body": "A HIPAA rule was struck down about a year after it took effect.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2025/06/hipaas-reproductive-health-rule-is-vacated-nationally", "label": "Holland & Knight, HIPAA's reproductive health rule vacated nationally"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In US health privacy, courts can undo a rule nationwide in a single decision.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2025/06/hipaas-reproductive-health-rule-is-vacated-nationally", "label": "Holland & Knight, HIPAA's reproductive health rule vacated nationally"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "A Texas federal court vacated the 2024 HIPAA reproductive health privacy rule nationwide on June 18, 2025.", "sectionKey": "rules"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$403bfbf1-3967-546b-b074-364627188bfc$ml$::uuid, $ml$healthtech$ml$, $ml$Selling a genetic database$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-18$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "healthtech-d18-career", "title": "Selling a genetic database", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "A bankruptcy put DNA data up for sale.", "eyebrow": "Day 18 · Where it breaks", "headline": "In 2025, a bankruptcy judge approved the sale of 23andMe's assets, including its genetic data, to a nonprofit led by co-founder Anne Wojcicki for $305 million.", "fullText": "Drugmaker Regeneron had won an earlier auction at $256 million. A group of 27 states and Washington, D.C., sued to block sales of customers' genetic data without explicit consent. California's attorney general said the deal did not comply with the state's genetic privacy law.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/judge-approves-23andme-sale-amid-privacy-dispute", "label": "MobiHealthNews, judge approves 23andMe sale amid privacy dispute"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "asset", "eyebrow": "Data as an asset", "text": "In bankruptcy, customer data can be sold like any other asset.", "highlight": "Here the data was DNA.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Genetic data", "definition": "Information from a person's DNA that can reveal health risks and family ties."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/judge-approves-23andme-sale-amid-privacy-dispute", "label": "MobiHealthNews, judge approves 23andMe sale amid privacy dispute"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "states", "eyebrow": "The pushback", "text": "27 states and D.C. argued genetic data is uniquely sensitive.", "highlight": "They wanted explicit consent before any sale.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/judge-approves-23andme-sale-amid-privacy-dispute", "label": "MobiHealthNews, judge approves 23andMe sale amid privacy dispute"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "breach", "eyebrow": "The backstory", "title": "A 2023 breach", "body": "A 2023 data breach had affected about seven million 23andMe users.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/judge-approves-23andme-sale-amid-privacy-dispute", "label": "MobiHealthNews, judge approves 23andMe sale amid privacy dispute"}]}, {"kind": "spotFake", "id": "fake", "prompt": "One of these is false. Tap it.", "statements": ["The winning bid was $305 million.", "All states supported the sale.", "Regeneron had bid $256 million earlier."], "fakeIndex": 1, "explanation": "27 states and D.C. sued, and several stayed opposed."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You lead a consumer health startup holding user DNA data.", "prompt": "What do you promise users?", "options": ["Consent before any data transfer", "Data may go to any future buyer", "Nothing, since terms can change"], "consequences": ["You build trust that survives a sale or failure.", "Users and states may push back hard.", "States fought 23andMe over just this."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "States pushed for explicit consent before genetic data could be sold."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Privacy beyond HIPAA", "body": "Consumer health data often falls under state laws. Privacy roles must know them.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/judge-approves-23andme-sale-amid-privacy-dispute", "label": "MobiHealthNews, judge approves 23andMe sale amid privacy dispute"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In consumer health, the data you collect can outlive the company that collected it.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/judge-approves-23andme-sale-amid-privacy-dispute", "label": "MobiHealthNews, judge approves 23andMe sale amid privacy dispute"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "A judge approved 23andMe's $305 million sale to a nonprofit led by Anne Wojcicki in 2025, despite challenges from 27 states and D.C.", "sectionKey": "my_view"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
