rl": "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/09/08/us-court-allows-particles-antitrust-claims-against-epic-to-proceed/", "label": "HIT Consultant, court allows Particle's antitrust claims against Epic"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "early", "eyebrow": "Still early", "title": "Allowed, not decided", "body": "Letting claims proceed means the case continues. It does not mean Epic has been found liable.", "sources": [{"url": "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/09/08/us-court-allows-particles-antitrust-claims-against-epic-to-proceed/", "label": "HIT Consultant, court allows Particle's antitrust claims against Epic"}]}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What did the court decide in September 2025?", "options": ["Epic was found liable", "Particle's core claims can proceed", "The case was fully dismissed"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "The court denied Epic's motion to dismiss the core monopolization claims."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your health data startup depends on access to Epic records.", "prompt": "How do you reduce risk?", "options": ["Use formal, regulated access", "Rely on one informal agreement", "Scrape data without permission"], "consequences": ["Formal routes are harder to cut off.", "Informal access can vanish overnight.", "You invite legal trouble."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Access through formal, regulated channels is more durable."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "David versus Epic", "body": "A small health data startup took the biggest EHR company to court.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/09/08/us-court-allows-particles-antitrust-claims-against-epic-to-proceed/", "label": "HIT Consultant, court allows Particle's antitrust claims against Epic"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In health data, whoever holds the records holds the power over who can build on them.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/09/08/us-court-allows-particles-antitrust-claims-against-epic-to-proceed/", "label": "HIT Consultant, court allows Particle's antitrust claims against Epic"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "A federal judge let Particle Health's core antitrust claims against Epic proceed in September 2025.", "sectionKey": "players"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d24f8739-ab53-57d7-ac3b-73dc357bf773$ml$::uuid, $ml$healthtech$ml$, $ml$The VA's costly EHR switch$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-22$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "healthtech-d22-career", "title": "The VA's costly EHR switch", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "A $10 billion contract became something far bigger.", "eyebrow": "Day 22 · The numbers", "headline": "The VA's Oracle Health EHR program began with a $10 billion contract in 2018, and its latest lifecycle cost estimate is about $37 billion.", "fullText": "A 2022 estimate by the Institute for Defense Analyses projected about $50 billion. By late 2025, only six of the VA's 170 medical centers used the new system. The VA paused most rollouts in April 2023 over safety and usability problems, then planned 13 more sites for 2026.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/modernization/2025/12/lawmakers-question-va-health-records-costs-and-batched-deployments/410188/?oref=ng-next-story", "label": "Nextgov, lawmakers question VA health record's costs"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "lifecycle", "eyebrow": "The metric", "text": "Lifecycle cost includes building, running and maintaining a system for years.", "highlight": "It is far larger than the first contract.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Lifecycle cost", "definition": "The total cost of a system over its whole life, including operation and upkeep."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/modernization/2025/12/lawmakers-question-va-health-records-costs-and-batched-deployments/410188/?oref=ng-next-story", "label": "Nextgov, lawmakers question VA health record's costs"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "progress", "eyebrow": "The progress", "text": "Six of 170 VA medical centers were live by late 2025.", "highlight": "That is under 4% of sites.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/modernization/2025/12/lawmakers-question-va-health-records-costs-and-batched-deployments/410188/?oref=ng-next-story", "label": "Nextgov, lawmakers question VA health record's costs"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "restart", "eyebrow": "The restart", "title": "Back on in 2026", "body": "The VA lifted its pause in December 2025 and planned four Michigan sites for April 2026, then nine more.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/modernization/2025/12/lawmakers-question-va-health-records-costs-and-batched-deployments/410188/?oref=ng-next-story", "label": "Nextgov, lawmakers question VA health record's costs"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-sites", "prompt": "How many of the VA's 170 medical centers used the new EHR by late 2025?", "min": 0, "max": 50, "value": 6, "unit": "", "tolerance": 0.06, "explanation": "Six, after rollouts were paused in April 2023."}, {"kind": "spotFake", "id": "fake", "prompt": "One of these is false. Tap it.", "statements": ["The original 2018 contract was $10 billion.", "The rollout finished on schedule in 2023.", "A 2022 estimate projected about $50 billion."], "fakeIndex": 1, "explanation": "Rollouts were paused in April 2023, with only six sites live by late 2025."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Implementation is hard", "body": "Big EHR rollouts need skilled implementation and training teams. The VA shows what is at stake.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/modernization/2025/12/lawmakers-question-va-health-records-costs-and-batched-deployments/410188/?oref=ng-next-story", "label": "Nextgov, lawmakers question VA health record's costs"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In health IT, the first contract price is rarely the real cost.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/modernization/2025/12/lawmakers-question-va-health-records-costs-and-batched-deployments/410188/?oref=ng-next-story", "label": "Nextgov, lawmakers question VA health record's costs"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "The VA's EHR program grew from a $10 billion contract to a roughly $37 billion lifecycle estimate, with six of 170 sites live by late 2025.", "sectionKey": "numbers"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
