highlight": "Developers can also lose certification.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.dlapiper.com/en-us/insights/publications/2025/09/hhs-steps-up-enforcement-on-health-information-blocking", "label": "DLA Piper, HHS steps up enforcement on information blocking"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "report", "eyebrow": "How it is reported", "title": "A public portal", "body": "Patients, providers and others can report suspected blocking through ONC's portal.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.dlapiper.com/en-us/insights/publications/2025/09/hhs-steps-up-enforcement-on-health-information-blocking", "label": "DLA Piper, HHS steps up enforcement on information blocking"}]}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Who faces fines of up to $1 million per violation?", "left": {"name": "Health IT developers and networks", "note": "Certified developers, HINs"}, "right": {"name": "Individual patients", "note": "Requesting records"}, "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Developers and health information networks face the $1 million penalties."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "Which law prohibits information blocking?", "options": ["The HITECH Act", "The 21st Century Cures Act", "The Affordable Care Act"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "The information blocking provisions come from the 21st Century Cures Act."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "A fine for hiding data", "body": "US health IT companies can be fined up to $1 million for each act of blocking data.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.dlapiper.com/en-us/insights/publications/2025/09/hhs-steps-up-enforcement-on-health-information-blocking", "label": "DLA Piper, HHS steps up enforcement on information blocking"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In US health data, blocking access is not just bad practice; it can be illegal.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.dlapiper.com/en-us/insights/publications/2025/09/hhs-step