ven EHRs pledged to \"kill the clipboard.\"", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/white-house-tech-leaders-commit-create-patient-centric-healthcare-ecosystem", "label": "CMS, tech leaders commit to a patient-centric health ecosystem"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "risk", "eyebrow": "The open question", "title": "Pledges need follow-through", "body": "Voluntary pledges depend on companies delivering. Results were targeted for early 2026.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/white-house-tech-leaders-commit-create-patient-centric-healthcare-ecosystem", "label": "CMS, tech leaders commit to a patient-centric health ecosystem"}]}, {"kind": "spotFake", "id": "fake", "prompt": "One of these is false. Tap it.", "statements": ["More than 60 companies made pledges.", "The pledges were binding federal mandates.", "Results were targeted for early 2026."], "fakeIndex": 1, "explanation": "CMS set voluntary criteria; participation is based on pledges."}, {"kind": "buildChain", "id": "chain", "prompt": "Put these interoperability milestones in order.", "steps": ["The 21st Century Cures Act passes", "TEFCA goes live", "Tech firms pledge to CMS's health ecosystem", "Pledged results are due"], "explanation": "2016, December 2023, July 2025, then the first quarter of 2026."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Killing the clipboard", "body": "Tech companies pledged to end repetitive paper forms at the doctor's office.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/white-house-tech-leaders-commit-create-patient-centric-healthcare-ecosystem", "label": "CMS, tech leaders commit to a patient-centric health ecosystem"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In health tech, voluntary pledges matter only if companies deliver on them.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/white-house-tech-leaders-commit-create-p