($ml$ffa378fb-058e-5850-9c80-3114c7ee088b$ml$::uuid, $ml$c2884709-56d2-54bf-a245-09e1c9b14f60$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 13 · HIPAA$ml$, $ml$By July 2022, the federal health privacy regulator had brought 38 enforcement actions against providers that failed to give patients their own records. HHS's Office for Civil Rights launched its Right of Access Initiative in 2019. Settlements in one batch ranged from $3,500 to $240,000. In one case, a podiatry practice paid a $100,000 penalty after ignoring a patient's request.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.techtarget.com/healthtechsecurity/news/366594714/OCR-Settles-11-HIPAA-Right-of-Access-Cases", "label": "TechTarget, OCR settles 11 HIPAA right of access cases"}]$ml$::jsonb),
