($ml$2ada29af-dfae-5553-961a-22f53f2812cf$ml$::uuid, $ml$403bfbf1-3967-546b-b074-364627188bfc$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In 2025, a bankruptcy judge approved the sale of 23andMe's assets, including its genetic data, to a nonprofit led by co-founder Anne Wojcicki for $305 million. Drugmaker Regeneron had won an earlier auction at $256 million. A group of 27 states and Washington, D.C., sued to block sales of customers' genetic data without explicit consent. California's attorney general said the deal did not comply with the state's genetic privacy law.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/judge-approves-23andme-sale-amid-privacy-dispute", "label": "MobiHealthNews, judge approves 23andMe sale amid privacy dispute"}]$ml$::jsonb),
