($ml$85c51cdf-67fb-55de-b5a1-fcc34ccf7d36$ml$::uuid, $ml$f3e4997c-f7bb-5faa-ab79-751a7ed32123$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 20 · The money$ml$, $ml$In June 2022, Oracle completed its acquisition of Cerner, the second-largest US hospital EHR vendor, for about $28.3 billion. Oracle paid $95 a share in cash. Cerner's systems ran in thousands of hospitals and clinics worldwide and became Oracle Health. By 2025, Oracle Health held 21.9% of US acute care hospitals and was losing hospitals to Epic.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.torys.com/en/work/2022/06/6f849441-8ab8-403f-ae7f-e548e5ea173a", "label": "Torys, Oracle completes acquisition of Cerner"}, {"url": "https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/healthcare-information-technology/ehrs/epic-up-by-77-hospitals-8-things-to-know/", "label": "Becker's, Epic up by 77 hospitals"}]$ml$::jsonb),
