($ml$3b054077-fbae-57c4-9e39-273895852245$ml$::uuid, $ml$2e4c01f2-8342-5a0a-94da-a91910d75a5d$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 24 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In early 2026, Epic released AI Charting, which listens during patient visits, drafts the clinician's note and queues up orders. It entered a market where Microsoft's Nuance and Abridge were described as dominant players. Investors had put about $1.6 billion into ambient AI companies in 2025 through September. Epic said 85% of its customers were already live with its generative AI tools.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/ai-and-machine-learning/epic-rolls-out-ai-charting-and-more-built-automation-clinicians-and", "label": "Fierce Healthcare, Epic's AI scribe goes live"}]$ml$::jsonb),
